Hello, folks...

I stumbled across something a bit, well, unusual while playing NH3.1.2
earlier today, I just had to share it with you.

As a little bit of background, I need to mention that, for a change of
pace, I decided to excavate Gehennom, digging out and lighting pretty
much every square inch, starting just below the Valley of the Dead all
the way to the bottom.  Actually acomplished it, too!  (ok, I'm wierd)

Anyway, after finishing that project, I attacked the Wizard's Tower and
cleaned out all but the uppermost level.  Noticing that some monsters
had been generated on a couple of the levels outside the tower, I decided
to eliminate them before returning top-side to drop off accumulated gold
and gems.  That's when I found the Long Worm from Hell (literally).

When I entered the level, I saw a long worm fully occupying the corridor
below the tower.  Moving to the other side, I discovered that a long
worm was fully occupying the corridor above the enclose, only I couldn't
see a head on this one.  Putting on my blindfold, I could only locate a
single worm-head.  I decided to lure the worm fully onto one side of the
tower to get a look at exactly how big the sucker was.  However, after
letting it chase me back and forth across the one side of the tower for
awhile, both corridors were still blocked and the side I was on was rapidly
filling.  Still curious as to how big it was, I reached into my BoH and
pulled out a couple cursed Teleport scrolls, popped up a few levels and
then back, and repeated until I was on the opposite side of the tower.

